From 5fdff78536d9948ae9c23f2fba32d69519cfd4db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:02:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): background notices flag `; echo EXIT=$?` masked
 failures [daveey]

A background `hermes chat -q ... > log 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?` printed EXIT=1, but the
shell's exit code was echo's 0 and the completion notice said "completed normally
(exit code 0)" (self-heal defect agent-1e03ea6be2).

Why: the notice text came from the exit code alone; the masked-success check that
foreground terminal results run (terminal_hints.annotate_masked_success) never ran
for background notices, and it only knew `| tail` / `|| echo` shapes with no rule for
a printed status line.

- terminal_hints: status-echo wrapper shape (trailing `; echo|printf ...$?`) paired
  with the LAST whole-line printed status in the output tail (EXIT=1, rc=1, exit
  code: 3, STATUS=127; nonzero only; read-only heads still excluded); `; true` /
  `; :` joins the masking shapes with the existing strong failure shapes.
- process_registry_notifications: a plain exit-0 completion whose command/output
  show a masked failure says "exited 0 but output shows failure" plus a Warning
  line (checked before the subagent trim); the UI title says "Exited 0 but Output
  Shows Failure". Exit codes are never changed.

Proof: 9 new tests red on 5ff44110acc, green after; 653 + 568 tests in the
notifier/hints/terminal/process_registry files pass.
